'''{{Keyword|unity|Unity}}''' is the 3rd major prestige layer in the game. It is reached when you have {{Keyword|ep|1.08e2466 EP}}.
When you {{Keyword|unity|Unite}}, you will be able to pick one of 4 Zodiacs from each element type: <span class="zodiacfire">Fire</span>, <span class="zodiacwind">Wind</span>, <span class="zodiacwater">Water</span>, or <span class="zodiacearth">Earth</span> <!-- Feels too walkthrough-ish imo. - ChillCatto -->

== Unity Bonuses ==
In the [[Unity#Astrology|Astrology]] tab, a panel displays passive bonuses that scale with your total number of Unities (Ʊ). These bonuses apply globally and increase important progression resources:

* {{Keyword|ip|IP Gain}} = <math>[1 + Unities] ^ {[ 2 + log(Unities) ]}</math>
* {{Keyword|ep|EP Gain}} = <math>[1 + Unities] ^ {[ 1 + 0.25 * log(Unities) ]}</math>
* {{Keyword|eternity|Σ (Eternity Count) Gain}} = <math>[1 + Unities]</math>
* {{Keyword|dp|DP Gain}} = <math>[1 + Unities * 3] ^ {[ 0.5 + 0.125 * log(Unities) ]}</math>

These bonuses are not tied to Zodiacs or Planets and are instead a direct reward for accumulating more Unities.

== Astrology ==
[[File:Astrology Tab.png|thumb|The Astrology tab]]
The Astrology system is the first of four core progression mechanics in {{Keyword|unity|Unity}}, alongside [[Trials]], [[Attacks]] and [[Relics]]. It revolves around acquiring and assigning <span class="zodiac">Zodiacs</span> to <span class="planet">Planets</span>, granting a wide variety of bonuses.

=== Zodiacs ===
<small>Main page: ''[[Zodiacs]]''</small>

Zodiacs are collectible entities in the Astrology system that provide bonuses when assigned to Planets. Each Zodiac belongs to one of four Elements — <span class="zodiacfire">Fire</span>, <span class="zodiacwind">Wind</span>, <span class="zodiacwater">Water</span>, or <span class="zodiacearth">Earth</span> — and corresponds to one of the four seasons.

There are 12 Zodiac signs in total. Each can have up to four possible bonuses unique to its sign and element group. Some bonuses are shared across signs of the same element.

The strength of each Zodiac's bonuses scales with its <span style="color: #eaac2d;">Quality</span>, <span style="color: #3f6af4;">Level</span>, and Rarity.

=== Planet Shop ===
<small>Main page: ''[[Planet Shop]]''</small><br>The planet shop is unlocked after the completion of Easy Trial 6. The Planet shop is a new place in the unity main page. The planet shop uses Astrodust to buy donuts, or use Zodiac modifiers. the 4 donuts you get to buy are <span style="color: #55c0f4;">'''Game speed'''</span>, <span style="color: #5cd236;">'''Luck'''</span>, <span style="color: #eaac2d;">'''Quality'''</span>, and <span style="color: #3f6af4;">'''Zodiac Exp. Factor'''</span>. The 4 zodiac modifiers you get access to are <span style="color: #af59e9;">'''Merging'''</span>, <span style="color: #87c200;">'''Enhancing'''</span> , <span style="color: #00ca8b;">'''Redistribution'''</span> and <span style="color: #db7c00;">'''Sacrificing'''</span>.

=== Planets ===
<small>Main page: ''[[Planets]]''</small><br>
Zodiacs must be assigned to Planets to activate their effects. This means that having a zodiac in the inventory does not automatically activate it’s effects.

A Zodiac placed on a Planet contributes:
* All its unlocked bonuses
* A Planet bonus, determined by the Zodiac’s Season

The combined effects of all Zodiacs placed on Planets are displayed under Zodiac bonuses in the Astrology tab.

Each Planet can only hold one Zodiac at a time. The cumulative effects of all Planet placements are listed in the Extra bonuses panel in the Astrology tab.

== Trials ==
Main page: ''[[Trials]]'' <br>Trials are the Unity version of eternity challenges. Each completed trial will give you a unique permanent reward and +2 default EC completions. when you complete all 6 trials of a certain difficulty, you will get another reward. There are 25 trials (as of V1.068) with 6 Easy Trials, 6 Medium trials, 6 Hard Trials, 6 Insane Trials and 1 Bonus Trial. When you want to attempt a trial, you should hit the lock and then reset your unity, forgetting to lock may lead to you accidentally breaking a trials condition. Remember to unlock the trial after you complete it!
[[File:Trial tab.png|none|thumb|296x296px|The Trial tab]]


== Relics ==
Main page: ''[[Relics]]'' <br>Relics are powerful artifacts that provide various bonuses across different game stages. Relics are purchased using Gold earned from Attack runs. As of update V1.068, there are a total of 7'''0''' unique relics, each unlocking at specific Attack levels.
[[File:Relics tab.png|none|thumb|The Relics tab]]

== Attacks ==
[[File:Attack Tab.png|thumb|The Attack tab]]
Main page: ''[[Attacks]]'' <br>
Attacks are unlocked after completing 15 [[Trials|trials]]. A new tab is added with a new revolution type, Attack Circles. For every Attack Level, there is an enemy, depicted as a HP bar in the middle of the screen. Your goal is to deal enough damage to deplete the enemy's HP bar and advance to the next Attack Level.

There are a total 5 Attack Circles and they work similarly to the base game's circles. Every revolution/lap increases the Attack Circle's Attack Damage Multiplier on the top of the screen. In addition, each revolution/lap counts as a hit to the enemy, dealing damage to its HP bar.

When you do a proper Unity by selecting a Zodiac, the Attack Level gets reset to 0 and you will be rewarded with the amount of Gold that is shown at the bottom of the screen. Your Circle Attack Multipliers will NOT be reset upon Uniting and performing a Soft Unity Reset (by e.g. swapping Zodiacs) will not reset Attack Level.

== Minerals ==
[[File:Mineral Footage.png|thumb|The Mineral tab]]
Main page: ''[[Minerals]]'' <br>Minerals are unlocked after completing {{Keyword|ach|Achievement 240}} (reach attacks level 1337), which adds a new subtab to the Unity tab. There are total of 100 minerals in the game, and each mineral generates a resource called '''Value Points (VP)'''. These can be used to buy VP upgrades. 

The base formula for VP gain is: <math> 0.01 \cdot 3 ^ {(Mineral Level - 1)} </math>

Upon reaching Mineral level 30, you can perform Polish Prestige. Doing this, you will gain '''Polish Points (PP)''' based on what level your highest mineral was (gains a boost every 5 levels, scales faster after lvl 50 Mineral). You can spend PP on 5 Weapons: Sword, Axe, Spear, Bow and Knuckles. Sword multiplies VP gain, Axe powers Mineral cost fall, Spear multiplies gold gain, Bow multiplies Attacks Ascension Power, and Knuckles boosts Minerals Local Speed exponent.

Upon reaching Mineral level 70, you can perform Refinement Prestige. Doing this, you will gain '''Refinement Points (RfP)''' based on what level your highest Mineral was (gains a boost every 10 levels). RfP can be used to buy nodes in the Refine Tree. There are 136 nodes, and some are upgradeable to certain levels, while most are single-time buy.

'''Magnets'''

Magnets are unlocked through {{Keyword|node|Refine Tree Node 18}}, giving a base 1% chance to obtain a magnet upon merging common minerals. Magnets also unlock Magnet Upgrades, giving buffs to minerals.

==== Runes ====
Runes are unlocked with {{Keyword|node|Refine Tree Node 35}} There are 2 types of runes: Sun and Moon runes. Both of these are generated over time, albeit very slowly. Their generation speed can be boosted with RfP, and each rune can be spent on 3 decent upgrades.

'''Special Minerals'''

Special Minerals are unlocked through {{Keyword|unknown|Refine Tree Node 41}}, unlocking a new grid of minerals. 1 special mineral can be spawned at a time at the cost of Sun and Moon Runes. There are 10 special minerals, Red boosts VP gain, Blue decreases cost increase, Green increases Cost Fall, Pink boost Luck & Quality, Yellow boost Gold Gain, Orange boosts Magnet Chance, Dark Purple boosts PP Gain, Light Blue boosts RfP Gain, White boosts Game Speed, and Black grants tarot draws when destroyed. Special Mineral Progression can also be unlocked through {{Keyword|unknown|Refine Tree Node 46}} where you can spend RfP to boost the effect of the other Gems.

==== Special Minerals Progression (SMP) ====
SMP is unlocked with {{Keyword|node|Refine Tree Node 46}}. Here, you can gain SMP EXP through merging Special Minerals, with each Special Mineral having its own SMP EXP counter. Once you have enough, your spawn level for that special mineral increases. Additionally, the efficiency of these minerals’ effects can be upgraded with RfP.

==== Special Mineral Sacrifice ====
Special Mineral Sacrifice is unlocked via {{Keyword|node|Refine Tree Node 85}}. After unlocking, you can ''sacrifice'' a special mineral by destroying 100 level 20 minerals of that type. Once sacrificed, you can no longer spawn that mineral, and you will instead be granted a level 27 version within the Sacrifice tab (equal to 128 level 20 minerals, more than a max grid). Once all special minerals have been sacrificed, spawning a special mineral will grant ''sacrifice dust'' instead, which can be used to level up sacrificed minerals.

== Elements ==
[[File:Elements tree.png|thumb|Element Trees]]
Main page: ''[[Elements]]'' <br>Elements are unlocked after completing {{Keyword|ach|Achievement 321}}, which adds a new sub-tab to the Unity tab. Here, you can generate 4 different Elements: '''{{Keyword|red|Fire}}''', '''{{Keyword|green|Earth}}''', '''{{Keyword|cyan|Wind}}''', and {{Keyword|blue|Water}}. '''You can only generate one element at a time.''' Each element’s generation is boosted by specific Factors, and your Global Element Multiplier. Each of these factors usually comes from the effects of Zodiacs of that element, like how Earth generation is boosted by your Infinity count. Additionally, each element can be spent on their respective Element Tree for powerful upgrades.  

== Tarot ==
Main page: ''[[Tarot]]'' <br>Tarot is unlocked after purchasing {{Keyword|node|Refine Tree Node 70}}, which adds a new subtab to the Unity tab. Unlocked along with Tarot are Black Gems, the 10th Special Mineral type. Destroying these will grant Tarot Draws, which can be used to draw Tarot Cards. These cards come in 5 suits: Swords, Wands, Pentacles, Cups, and a special Arcana suit. For the 4 regular suits, each card boosts a specific stat, and this boost gets better the more copies, or levels, of that card you have. The arcana cards can be used as a sort-of power up, each one providing a boost when activated, and requiring a long cooldown before it can be used again. In total, there are 78 unique cards; 14 for the regular suits, and 22 Arcan cards.

==== Upgrades ====
Each of these 4 regular suits has their respective resource, generated by the Ace card and boosted by the other cards in that suit. With 1,000,000 of each, you unlock Tarot Upgrades where you can spend these resources on many powerful upgrades.

==== Challenges ====
Unlocked with Refine Tree Node 89, these are very similar to the other challenge systems from before. Each Tarot card has its own respective challenge, and you start with the first card of every suit. More challenges are unlocked with each completion of a new challenge, and each one gives a boost to the respective card’s effect.

==== Artifacts ====
Artifacts are unlocked through {{Keyword|node|Refine Tree Node 99}}. Here, you can convert regular Tarot Resources into their golden version with the flush button. Doing so will instantly grant the golden resources, though a ^0.001 resource generation penalty will be incurred that gradually weakens over time. Each golden resource has its own Artifact, which comes in multiple parts. These parts must be unlocked by having enough of a specific Golden Resource. Each part provides powerful boosts, and can be further leveled up with Golden Resources. (Note: you do not spend any of the resources, you just need to have enough to get the upgrade.)

== Plague ==
Main page ''[[Plague]]'' <br>
Plague is unlocked after purchasing {{Keyword|node|Refine Tree Node 103}}, which adds a new sub-tab to the Unity tab. Here, you can infect many populations inside certain locations, or Plague Stage. Successfully completing a Plague Stage will reward Plague Generators, or PlG. These generate Plague Points, or PlP. These resources and other statistics like your highest stage cleared, total infected, etc. boost many aspects of the game.

==== Endoplasmic Reticulum ====
Unlocked through Refine Tree Node 104, you can craft Endoplasmic Reticulums (ERs) using your PlP. These are basically different plague strains, and have 3 different stats: Spread Power, Infectivity, and Stealth. Spread Power determines overall speed, Infectivity allows for faster spreading during the middle stage of infection, and stealth decreases the slowdown caused by the remaining healthy population.

Unwanted ERs can be dissolved for Virus Essence, which generates Virus Points, or ViP that can be spent on upgrades that boost your ERs.

== Singularity ==
Main page ''[[Singularity]]'' <br>
Singularity is unlocked after purchasing {{Keyword|node|Refine Tree Node 121}}, which adds a new subtab to the Unity tab. Singularity is centered around Atoms, which multiply themselves every second based on your Singularity Multiplier. This multiplier can be increased by performing a Singularity, which resets the following:

* Minerals (except the Refine Tree)
* Elements
* Tarot (except Tarot Upgrades and Challenges)
* Plague
* Your current Atom Count

After your first singularity, you will need 1.8e308 Atoms to perform a Singularity again.

==== Milestones ====
Unlocked with your first Singularity, you can collect Milestone rewards by achieving a certain amount of Singularities or Atoms. Additionally, there are Progression milestones, which inflict penalties until a specific requirement is satisfied, in which the penalty disappears and is replaced with a buff.

==== Effects ====
Unlocked with your second Singularity, each of your Singularity Count, Atoms amount, and Singularity Multiplier will provide powerful boosts. More effects can be unlocked the more you progress.

==== Tree ====
Unlocked at 5 Singularities, the Tree allows you to purchase upgrades out of an upgrade tree consisting of 13 nodes using Atoms. Unlike many other upgrades, a purchase will divide your atom count instead of subtracting. Each upgrade can be purchased up to level 10, in which it can be Ascended. Doing so will reset the level but not the effect, though the effect scales slower after and the cost increases faster.

==== Houses ====
Houses are unlocked at 32 Singularities, and it functions like an advanced version of Astrology. However, each Zodiac can only be placed in its matching House, and they can only be obtained by performing a Singularity with more than 1e1000 Atoms. Each of these zodiacs provide unique buffs to many aspects of your progression.

== Trivia ==

* On your first {{Keyword|unity|Unity}}, you will be guaranteed the option of a Lv3 Rare <span class="zodiacfire">Aries</span> with 2 buffs: common exponent and mult gain

